  "body": "Sea views, room to move and a coastal setting that makes everyday life feel a little different. Set across multiple levels in Waiake, this substantial six-bedroom home offers 440m² of floor area on an 800m² section. With three bathrooms, multiple living areas and extraordinary garaging, there's flexibility here for larger households and changing needs.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, soaring ceilings, exposed timber beams and expansive windows give the living room a sense of openness, with sweeping sea views providing a coastal backdrop. The adjoining dining area and kitchen create an inviting setting for shared meals, while a balcony extends the outlook outdoors. Downstairs, a second kitchen, breakfast nook and family room offer flexibility, with easy access to the patio. Separate laundry facilities on both levels add everyday convenience.\r\n\r\nSix bedrooms are distributed across the home, including a primary bedroom with a walk-in wardrobe and access to the front balcony. Three further bedrooms occupy the upper level, while two downstairs provide options for guests, extended family or working from home. Three bathrooms, additional toilets and a separate room or office beside the lower garage add to the home's versatility.\r\n\r\nThe 800m² section offers established greenery, mature trees and a generous lawn for outdoor games or relaxed afternoons. Multiple balconies and patios provide places to enjoy the coastal outlook, while the covered patio offers a sheltered retreat. A six-car garage arrangement, additional off-street parking and dedicated storage are appealing for vehicle enthusiasts or anyone needing extra room for equipment.\r\n\r\nWaiake brings the best of North Shore coastal living within easy reach, from Waiake Beach and Torbay village cafés to Long Bay Regional Park. Torbay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College are also nearby. With its scale, outlook and adaptable layout, this is a home worth exploring. Contact Darren Young to arrange your viewing and discover what life at 4 Newburn Road could look like.",
